cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite Zou, Ju and Carr, and CASSIE.
title: multipolygon_triangulator (MWT) for curvenet.elf (vendored)
abstract: >-
  All 18 files of thirdparty/multipolygon_triangulator in the org's Godot
  fork, 94,889 bytes before this file: DMWT and MingCurve, Ming
  Zou's triangulator for multiple 3D polygons (SGP 2013, v1.1.0) as adapted
  by Tibor Stanko and Emilie Yu for CASSIE, plus the fork's DelaunayFaces
  (3D Delaunay through Geogram "BDEL"). DMWT.cpp's coplanar branch calls
  cassie::delaunay_triangulate_2d_raw (vendor/cassie/src/delaunay_geogram),
  which builds in the same library. tools/vendor/thirdparty_subset.sh
  reproduces the tree from the pinned commit. Local adaptation
  (tools/vendor/patches/mwt.patch): DMWT.cpp includes <climits> for
  INT_MAX, which it used to receive through the Godot-typed
  delaunay_geogram.h that the Cassie subset rewrote include-free; and
  Point3::pertube draws 0..9999 as mt19937's raw output modulo 10000
  instead of through std::uniform_int_distribution, whose algorithm
  differs between libc++ (the native flat control) and libstdc++ (the
  guest), so degenerate input was perturbed differently on each.
type: software
